>> title: Teriyaki Ginger Beef Stir-Fry
>> servings: 3


== Beef ==
> Note: this technique is called "velvetting" and it can be done with more than just beef!
In a #medium bowl{}, combine @beef strips{1%lb} and @baking soda{2%tsp}. Mix together well so that the baking soda fully coats the beef without excess.

Refrigerate the beef strips for ~{45%minutes} while they velvet. During the last few minutes of velvetting, prepare the sauce.

Remove the beef from the refrigerator and rinse off all the baking soda. Pat the beef dry.

In a #medium sized pan{}, add @olive oil{2%tbsp} and heat over medium-high heat. Add the beef to the pan once the oil is hot, stirring occasionally with a #rubber spatula{}.

When the beef is mostly browned, add in @ginger{1%thumb}(minced) and @garlic{2%cloves}(minced). Sautee the ginger and garlic with the beef while it finishes cooking. 

Once the beef is cooked and the ginger & garlic is fragrant, add the prepared sauce to the pan and toss/stir to fully coat the beef. Continue cooking to reduce the sauce. Optionally, at this stage you can add in @broccoli{0.5%cup}(florets) to cook while the sauce reduces. 

== Sauce ==

> The white vinegar could probably be subtituted with rice vinegar or mirin
In a #small bowl{}, add @soy sauce{6%tbsp}, @sugar{0.25%cup}(granulated, white), @white vinegar{2%tbsp}, @corn starch{1%tsp}, @red pepper flakes{0.25%tsp}, and @black pepper{0.25%tsp}. Stir to combine and set aside.